# Profile: eval-runner

Runs one eval set from the phone and reports it. Taken from Steward's spec 002 (the
operator's first profile, 2026-11-08). Two tools, no reads before the card, low
reasoning, one plan card, and a summary line for the phone.

Its reach is what its two tools reach and nothing more: it can start an eval run and
read the run's status. It cannot read a file, run a shell or write a note, because it
is not offered a tool that does.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "eval-runner",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "run an eval set from the phone and report it",
    "capabilities": ["N8"]
  },
  "tools": ["secondbrain_eval_start", "secondbrain_eval_status"],
  "instructions": "Plan one secondbrain_eval_start with the set and the tag the request names. Ask nothing else.\nAfter the card, read secondbrain_eval_status once. Report passed of total and each failed check.",
  "budgets": { "reads": 0, "tool_calls": 4 },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["keys", "archive", "untrusted-shell", "sitting"],
    "extra": ["no set other than the one named"]
  },
  "card": "plan",
  "success": { "check": "tool_call_args_match" },
  "summary": "<set> <tag>: <passed>/<total>, failed: <case ids>"
}
```
